-- title:
--   Commutativity Points
-- statement:
--   **Commutativity of point-measurement products.**
--
--   Let $S$ be a symmetric strategy for the low individual degree test with parameters $(q,m,d)$ and normalized state $\psi$. Assume that its axis-parallel, self-consistency, and diagonal-line test failure probabilities are bounded by $\varepsilon$, $\delta$, and $\gamma$. For uniformly sampled points $u,v\in\mathbb{F}_q^m$, define the ordered point product by $P_L(u,v)_{a,b}=(A^u_aA^v_b)\otimes I$ and the reversed product by $P_R(u,v)_{a,b}=(A^v_bA^u_a)\otimes I$. Then
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}_{\psi,\mathcal U_{(\mathbb{F}_q^m)^2}}\!\left(P_L,P_R;\,32m\gamma\right).
--   $$
--
--   Thus the average state-dependent squared operator distance between the two ordered products is at most the diagonal-test loss multiplied by $32m$. This is the main commutativity-points theorem and is the point-level hypothesis consumed by `comMain` in the full-slice commutativity argument.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.CommutativityPoints.commutativityPoints`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/CommutativityPoints/BridgeTheorems/DropBridges.lean#L293-L393

